WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.650
Chapter 07 of the workbook names the
dangers, and the guard against each.

2
00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:09.228
A password copied into a report turns
the scan's output into a secret store,

3
00:00:09.228 --> 00:00:14.387
so the kit masks every password, and a test
checks that no fixture password appears.

4
00:00:14.387 --> 00:00:17.923
The password mode counted as
done would leave a deprecated

5
00:00:17.923 --> 00:00:21.387
flow that can't do M F A in
production, so the finding names it.

6
00:00:21.387 --> 00:00:25.571
Active Directory Default in production
makes the first connection slow,

7
00:00:25.571 --> 00:00:29.137
and the identity can change with
host settings, so name the mode.

8
00:00:29.137 --> 00:00:32.028
Every application on a host
shares the Arc identity,

9
00:00:32.028 --> 00:00:35.725
so one login's grants cover everything
allowed to ask for the token.

10
00:00:35.725 --> 00:00:39.958
Keep the Hybrid Agent Extension Applications
group to the accounts that need it,

11
00:00:39.958 --> 00:00:43.875
and give an application its own service
principal where its grants differ.

12
00:00:43.875 --> 00:00:47.496
And a string changed before the
gates hold fails at sign-in,

13
00:00:47.496 --> 00:00:50.380
so Lab 2 checks gates one
to three, in that order.
